      en: 'At the northern end of the Mainamati ridge, towards Burichang, a high mound is known as Rani Mainamati’s Palace. In folklore Queen Mainamati was the wife of King Manikchandra of the Chandra line and the mother of King Gopichandra; the ballads about Mainamati and Gopichandra are a well-known part of Bengali folk literature, and the whole ridge is said to take its name from her.\n\nExcavations have revealed the foundations of buildings from several different phases, thought to date from different periods. The brick walls, the lines of enclosure and the shape of the mound hint at a substantial structure in the past.\n\nThe site is quiet and seldom crowded. From the top the views over the surrounding plains and villages are lovely, especially on a clear winter day.',
