      en: 'Beside the Feni–Chhagalnaiya road at Chandgazi bazaar stands the eighteenth-century Chand Gazi Bhuiyan Mosque. Tradition says it was built by a local landholder, Chand Gazi Bhuiyan, who gave his name to both the mosque and the area. It is listed as a protected monument by the Department of Archaeology.\n\nThree domes rise above a rectangular prayer hall, with arched doorways in front and turrets at the corners — the familiar pattern of the Mughal style. The thin old bricks and the lines of the arches show their age, yet the building still stands firm.\n\nDaily prayers are held here, so the mosque remains part of local everyday life. Being close to the highway, it makes an easy short trip from Feni town.',
