      en: 'Near the mouth of the Little Feni river in Companiganj, Noakhali, the Musapur Closure is essentially a dam and regulator built to keep out tidal salt water and control drainage. Over time the wide chars, casuarina groves and open water around it have given Noakhali its own taste of a “beach.”\n\nRows of casuarina and other trees planted by the Forest Department, grassy chars and water stretching to the horizon make the place open and breezy. At low tide you can walk out across the char; at high tide the water creeps close.\n\nFamilies and young people pour in during the afternoon, and at sunset the water and sky light up with colour. River erosion and floods regularly change the landscape here, so it is wise to check local conditions before you go.',
